.\" Manual page for lantern(1). Keep in sync with daemon/lantern/cli.py and docs/CLI.md;
.\" tests/test_smoke.py checks that every command and option of the parser is described here.
.\" Preview: man ./docs/lantern.1    Lint: mandoc -T lint docs/lantern.1
.TH LANTERN 1 2026-10-19 "Lantern 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lantern \- local, offline semantic search for files, code, PDFs, photos and recordings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lantern
.RB [ \-h ]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lantern
indexes folders on this Mac and finds files by meaning and by exact words:
text, code (down to the line of a definition), PDFs (page), photos (what they show and the text in them) and
recordings (the moment something is said).
Everything runs locally with EmbeddingGemma 2 on Apple silicon; after the one-time model download nothing leaves
the Mac and indexed files are only ever read.
.PP
Most commands talk to the Lantern daemon over its Unix socket when it is running (started by the menu bar app,
.BR "lantern daemon run" ,
or the LaunchAgent): searches then take milliseconds and indexing continues in the background.
Without a daemon,
.BR index ,
.BR search ,
.BR remove ,
.BR compact ,
.BR clear\-history ,
.BR exclude ,
.BR ignore ,
.BR config ,
.B open
and
.B status
work on the index directly
.RB ( search
loads the model first, which takes a few seconds);
.BR pending ,
.BR approve ,
.BR decline ,
.B pause
and
.B resume
need the daemon.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Indexing
.TP
.BI "index " path " \fR[\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-transcribe\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]"
Add a folder or bring it up to date: new and changed files are indexed, moved files keep their vectors, deleted
files are removed with all their data.
An unavailable folder (unplugged disk, network share) is never purged.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-force
allow the update when more than half of the folder's indexed files are gone from the disk (refused otherwise).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-transcribe
without a daemon: index audio and video by sound only, without Whisper transcripts.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
read only names and sizes: counts per kind, folders without access and a rough time estimate; nothing is read or
written.
.RE
.TP
.BI "remove " path
Remove an indexed folder and everything derived from it, then compact the database so the data is erased from the
file.
.TP
.B compact
Physically erase deleted data from the index file (VACUUM, FTS optimize, WAL checkpoint).
.SS Searching
.TP
.BI "search " query " \fR[\fB\-n\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-only\fR \fIkind\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-log\fR]"
Search by meaning and keywords in one ranking.
Results come in sections (Definitions, Photos, Files) with their location:
.IR path : start \- end
for text and code,
.I path
(page
.IR N )
for PDFs,
.I path
@
.IR m : ss
for recordings.
The sources in brackets
.RI ( "meaning #k" ,
.IR "keywords #k" ,
.IR "image #k" )
show why each result matched.
Case, accents and letters such as \(/l, \(/o and \(ss are ignored; numbers and codes with separators must match
as a whole.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-limit " \fIN\fR"
number of results in the files section (default 10).
.TP
.BI \-\-only " kind"
only one kind of result:
.BR apps ,
.BR settings ,
.BR shortcuts ,
.BR code ,
.BR docs ,
.BR pdf ,
.BR photos ,
.B media
(recordings and videos) or
.B music
(Apple Music songs and playlists, sent by the app).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-log
do not record this search in the local history.
.RE
.TP
.BI "open " n " \fR[\fB\-\-reveal\fR | \fB\-\-print\fR]"
Open result
.I n
of the last search with its default app and record the choice in the local history.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-reveal
show it in Finder instead.
.TP
.B \-\-print
only print
\fIpath\fR[:\fIline\fR][ @ \fIm\fR:\fIss\fR],
for scripts and editors.
.RE
.TP
.B clear\-history
Delete the local search history and compact the database.
.SS Daemon
.TP
.BR "daemon run" | install | uninstall | stop " [\fB\-\-print\fR]"
.B run
starts the daemon in the foreground;
.B install
writes and starts the LaunchAgent
.RI ( ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.lantern.daemon.plist ,
started at every login);
.B "install \-\-print"
only prints that plist;
.B uninstall
removes it;
.B stop
asks a running daemon to stop after the current file.
The menu bar app starts its own daemon, so the LaunchAgent is optional.
.TP
.B status
Daemon, power (battery, Low Power Mode, thermal state), queue, files and folders; without a daemon a shorter report
of the index itself.
.TP
.B pending
Files the daemon found that wait for approval (in
.B ask
mode).
.TP
.B approve
Index the waiting files.
.TP
.B decline
Leave them until the next change.
.TP
.B pause
Pause background indexing (search keeps working).
.TP
.B resume
Resume background indexing.
.SS Settings
.TP
.BR config " [\fIkey\fR [\fIvalue\fR]]"
List the settings, or change one (booleans accept true/false, 1/0, yes/no).
Keys:
.BR index_mode " (" ask | auto ),
.BR pause_on_battery ,
.BR pause_on_low_power ,
.BR pause_on_thermal ,
.BR index_photos ,
.BR index_image_text ,
.BR places ,
.BR people ,
.BR index_audio_video ,
.BR transcribe ,
.BR index_video_frames ,
.BR notify ,
.BR debounce_s .
.TP
.BR exclude " " add | remove | list " [\fIpattern\fR]"
Extra exclusions on top of the defaults (.git, node_modules, build and cache folders, secrets such as .env*,
*.pem, id_*) and .gitignore: an absolute path (~ allowed) or a .gitignore-style pattern.
.TP
.BR ignore " " add | remove | list " [\fIextension\fR ...]"
File extensions never indexed (default .ipynb .csv .tsv);
.BR csv ,
.B .csv
and
.B *.csv
mean the same.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help (also after any command).
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LANTERN_HOME
Data folder instead of
.IR "~/Library/Application Support/Lantern" .
.TP
.B LANTERN_SOCKET
Socket path instead of
.IR $LANTERN_HOME/lantern.sock
(at most 104 bytes).
.TP
.B LANTERN_MEDIA
Path to
.B lantern\-media
(AVFoundation decoder; set by the app, otherwise
.I /Applications/Lantern.app
or
.IR app/build ;
.B off
forces
.BR ffmpeg ).
.TP
.B LANTERN_FFMPEG
Path to ffmpeg for MKV/WebM fallback (otherwise PATH, then the Homebrew locations).
.TP
.B LANTERN_NOTIFY
.B 0
turns notifications off.
.TP
.B LANTERN_WORKER_PRIORITY
.B background
(default) runs the indexing process with the background policy; any other value keeps normal priority.
.TP
.B LANTERN_EMBEDDER
.B fake
uses deterministic fake models, for tests and for trying the commands without models.
.PP
The model libraries always run offline; Lantern sets
.BR HF_HUB_OFFLINE ,
.B TRANSFORMERS_OFFLINE
and the telemetry opt-outs itself.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/Lantern/index.db
The index (SQLite with FTS5 and sqlite-vec). It holds text passages and vectors of the indexed files: treat it like
a copy of them.
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/Lantern/config.toml
Settings.
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/Lantern/lantern.sock
The daemon's API socket (mode 0600), present while it runs: newline-delimited JSON, one request per connection.
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/Lantern/logs/
Daemon logs: paths and errors, never file contents or queries.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/huggingface/hub/
Downloaded models.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error: the daemon is needed but not running, the folder is unavailable, the deletion guard refused, an unknown
setting, no such result.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments.
.TP
.B 3
.B index
finished, but some files failed (they are retried next time).
.SH EXAMPLES
Index a folder, then search it:
.PP
.RS
.nf
lantern index ~/Projects
lantern search "retry with exponential backoff"
lantern search "def add_two(x, y):" \-n 5
lantern search "invoice october" \-\-only pdf
.fi
.RE
.PP
Open the first result in VS Code at its line:
.PP
.RS
.nf
code \-g "$(lantern open 1 \-\-print)"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Try the commands on an isolated instance, without models and without touching the real index:
.PP
.RS
.nf
export LANTERN_HOME=/tmp/lantern\-try LANTERN_SOCKET=/tmp/lantern\-try.sock
export LANTERN_EMBEDDER=fake
lantern daemon run &
lantern index ~/some/folder && lantern search "anything"
lantern daemon stop
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mdfind (1)
.PP
The full reference with output formats and the socket API: docs/CLI.md in the repository,
https://github.com/misterekkk/lantern
